KG42.register("clusters-68819257295f59af5faf36ad",{"id":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v142-d-CL006","paper":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading","label":"Net expenditure and payment/receipt accounting for equilibrium transactions","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL006","label":"Net expenditure and payment/receipt accounting for equilibrium transactions","market_meaning":"Within the scope of the Case 6 equilibrium local solution, net expenditure is explained using purchased and sold energy, the supplier set, and optimal prices, including production cost, transportation cost, electricity-purchase expenditure, and electricity-sale revenue. General purchase-and-sale payments and receipts retain their economic interpretation; network-operator fees and taxes are only an optional component of transportation cost.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["settlement","pricing","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The detailed net-expenditure formula is limited to Case 6 and the local solution corresponding to the optimal prices; the quantity interface with the global configuration requires selecting the same feasible optimal solution. R010's iterative update and the four-microgrid Case 4 example retain their original scope and are not converted into universal settlement prices. The zero-flow transportation-cost convention still has a mathematical gap.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The clearing price and transaction quantity jointly give the accounting obligation and are suitable for reference across configuration, pricing, and payment chains; this net expenditure includes production cost and cannot be treated directly as the amount of a single external transfer. The actual payment execution procedure has not yet been provided.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the economic interpretation of payments and receipts, optional fees and taxes, and the Case 6 net-expenditure expression."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References the Case 6 optimal purchase and sale prices and the supplier set, retaining their other conditional content."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References feasible transaction quantities, scalar electricity-sale coordinates, and common cost inputs, limiting the consistent scope between accounting quantities and configuration."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL006-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X004","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X005","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T006","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-lambda-i","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-lambda-j","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g35-e035"],"rationale":"The prices and supplier set in the same Case 6 optimal solution are used to explain net expenditure; the optimal variables of the pricing chain are used as given parameters in the accounting chain, and the roles remain separate."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL006-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-Eij","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-eps","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-Eji","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-eps","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g17-e017","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The purchase-and-sale coordinates are associated only for the same feasible optimal solution; a generic directed flow must be relabeled as supplier j to buyer i. This interface does not prove the existence of metering confirmation or actual transfer."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL006-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-Ci","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-gamma","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-Ci","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-gamma","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-e007","v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g17-e017","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The system configuration and local accounting share production and transportation costs, but local net expenditure also includes transaction payments and revenue; the two are not deduplicated as the same objective expression."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X004","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-lambda-i"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g23-e023"],"rationale":"Limited to the seller i price in the same Case 6 equilibrium solution; the roles of optimal price variable and accounting valuation parameter are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X005","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-lambda-j"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e023"],"rationale":"Limited to the purchase price under the same supplier j and Case 6 equilibrium solution; the different local roles of pricing and accounting are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-eps","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-eps"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"Associates scalar electricity-sale quantity only at the same optimal feasible solution; an arbitrary local iterative offer is not recognized as a settled sale."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-Ci","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-Ci"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-e007","v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"All are the production cost function of the same microgrid; the roles in the system objective and local accounting are retained, and it is not merged with the example's common cost function."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-gamma","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-gamma"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-e007","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The source explicitly shares the same link transportation cost function; the optional fees-and-taxes interpretation does not constitute another determined tax rate."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-Ec","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-Ec"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-e004","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The fixed load under the same dispatch interval, microgrid, and equilibrium case; the configuration and accounting bindings are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X007","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-Eji"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e023"],"rationale":"The electricity-purchase quantity from supplier j to buyer i in the same Case 6 optimal local solution; the marginal price relation and accounting billing role are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-OM08","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::clearing.inter_area","v141-c-R010::V::clearing.inter_area"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::clearing.inter_area","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g24-e024"],"rationale":"All reference the same clearing function; the display selection does not equate its objective with the local net-expenditure expression."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL006-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The Case 6 net-expenditure formula records transportation cost only for the supplier set, whereas local objective (7) records cost by connection component; the current C does not explicitly carry the zero-flow cost convention. The wording elsewhere in the source that zero-flow cost is zero and that costs are generally positive also needs verification; it cannot be assumed by default that the cost of an unselected supplier automatically disappears.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-gamma","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-e007","v141-b-g11-e011","v141-b-g17-e017","v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the value of zero-flow cost, the general cost assumption, and the summation range, and have upstream clarify the complete applicability conditions of the accounting formula; D retains the existing formulas."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL006-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R012 provides the net-expenditure accounting formula but does not give payment execution timing, metering confirmation, tax rates, or collection procedures; the supplier set is also not declared as a parameter reference of this chain itself.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T006","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-e007","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g35-e035","v141-b-g02-e022"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually confirm the cross-chain supplier-set interface; if complete settlement execution rules or formal closure within the chain are required, sourced objects and processes must be supplemented upstream."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL006-G03","category":"unverified_source","description":"The net expenditure, optimal prices, and cost interpretation are all based on unaudited citations permitted by the experiment; this cannot be used to claim that the scientific content of settlement has independently passed review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-e007","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e023"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check item by item the accounting signs, optimal-solution scope, supplier set, and cost conventions; maintain B's unverified status."}]},"rule_refs":["27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R012","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R010","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-29875534ea059f1d","COMP-29a9bef8bb03bc72","COMP-30140116c1d9cc29","COMP-cb8f993b6ad4c7bc","KG40-7b5176e5e40aa7c7","KG40-ae777dabd8002658"]});
